#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""tools/cite_check.py: the citation leg (#43; docs/DESIGN.md §10; S4b's file, and only S4b's: C11 of C3's lens 3).

WHAT IT CHECKS. Every `file:line` citation in `lean/` and `docs/` (the Lean docstrings and comments, the pages) is
found by its shape (`<path>.<ext>:<N>` or `:<N>–<M>`, a `/`-list of further lines after it) and resolved to the
source it cites AT THE PIN: the pinned repositories of `docs/PROVENANCE.md` §1a (the reference bitcoin-sv, Teranode,
GoBDK, bsv-rs, go-sdk, the ts-sdk monorepo, go-chaincfg, the two pattern sources), read with `git show <commit>:<path>`,
never a working tree. A citation into a pinned source is ANCHORED by a row of the table at the end of this file: the
row names the site, the citation as written, the target (`repo@commit:path`, the lines) and a grep anchor, either a
SYMBOL that must occur within the cited lines (`sym`) or the exact text of the first and last cited lines (`text`). The
leg is RED when an anchored citation's anchor is no longer where the citation says, at the pin (a re-pin, a file the
resolution now finds elsewhere, a row edited by hand): "the leg RED when a cited line moves" (#43).

WHAT IT REPORTS AND NEVER TURNS RED. A citation no row anchors yet (`unanchored`: a page's new citation; `--propose`
writes its row, unless the table's owner HELD it at review: a citation read at another release than the pin, which a
row would anchor on the wrong lines; `HELD` below); a row whose citation left its site (`orphan`: the page was re-cut; `--propose` drops it); a citation
the resolver cannot place (`unresolved`: no pinned file ends with the path; `ambiguous`: two do and the context does not
choose; `beyond-eof`: the lines do not exist at the pin, a citation error for the page's owner); the citations into this
repository's own files (`self`: not a pinned source; their lines move with every edit; a bare name this repository also
tracks, `lakefile.toml` or a shim's `main.go`, is `self` unless its paragraph names a pinned source holding that name)
and citations in excluded sites under `docs/records/`, `docs/audit/` and `docs/BLOCKS-ARCHIVE.md` (`history`: a record, a filed lens report and an
archived block, moved out of HANDOFF §0 byte for byte by D125, are never edited, so their citations stand at their own
commit and a re-pin moves none of them; #47's move to bsv-rs 0.3.30 moved eight audit citations of 0.3.28's
`spend.rs`, which no page could re-cut), and into `docs/security/` (a private advisory's draft, once filed, is the copy
of what was sent, D135; under A28 the drafts stay off `main`, so there the rule reads an absent directory and keeps a
branch that holds them GREEN), and into `docs/recon.md` (the recon log, #39: each dated entry reads the upstreams at its
own day's releases, most of them beyond the pins, and a later pin re-cuts no entry). History sites are excluded BEFORE
opening, each counted by name as "closed to model turns, not opened". Their citations are not scanned and existing anchor
rows are retained as unchecked history, never treated as vanished citations. The proposal's findings are listed too: a citation whose
backticked neighbour symbol does not occur in the cited lines but does occur near them (`near-miss`), the class C2's S2
lens found by hand ("two citation ranges off by two lines at about twenty sites", #43's Why).

WHERE IT RUNS. The Studio and the box, where the clones are; in the Modal container every absent clone is SKIPPED BY
NAME and counted (never a pass), as `tools/check_pins.py` does. `CITE_CHECK_REQUIRE_CLONES=1` turns every skip into RED.

Usage:
  tools/cite_check.py                  the leg (exit 1 when an anchored citation moved; the counts on the last line)
  tools/cite_check.py --list           every citation found, with its resolution and its row
  tools/cite_check.py --propose        what `--write` would do: rows for the unanchored, the orphans dropped, the findings
  tools/cite_check.py --propose --write  rewrite the table below (the owner reviews the diff; a row may be edited by
                                       hand: its anchor and its kind are the owner's to choose)
  tools/cite_check.py --repin reference.commit=<sha> [--repin …]   the leg with a pin of §1a replaced IN MEMORY: every
                                       citation a re-pin would move, listed (the worklist a re-pin issue must re-read,
                                       docs/PROVENANCE.md's rule at the top); nothing is written
"""
import json
import os
import re
import subprocess
import sys
from collections import Counter, OrderedDict

ROOT = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))
SELF = os.path.abspath(__file__)

# the citation's shape: a path ending in a source extension, a colon, a line or a range; a `/`-list may follow
EXT = r"(?:cpp|cc|c|h|hpp|go|rs|ts|mjs|js|py|lean|md|toml|json|conf|sh|in|yml|yaml)"
CITE = re.compile(r"(?<![\w/.@-])((?:[\w.@-]+/)*[\w.-]*\w\." + EXT + r"):(\d+)(?:\s?[–-]\s?(\d+))?((?:/:?\d+(?:[–-]\d+)?)*)")
EXTRA = re.compile(r"/:?(\d+)(?:[–-](\d+))?")
